      "narrative": "Mara Venn tilts her head, a faint crease forming between her brows as she considers your question.\n\n\"Before it was sealed?\" She taps a finger on the table. \"Same man who's sitting over there now. Toran Vex has been the lock-keeper for the Ash Gate for going on six years. The Kestrel Guild contracted him to maintain the mechanism \u2014 oil the tumblers, check the hinges, make sure nothing jammed.\"\n\nShe jerks her chin toward the nervous clerk. \"He'd go out there every tenday, rain or shine, with his little leather kit of tools. Kept meticulous records, too \u2014 I've seen him scribbling in a ledger. Bram used to say Toran's logs were more detailed than the Guild's own manifests.\"\n\nA pause. She frowns slightly.\n\n\"That's the strange part, actually. The night Bram died, Toran's ledger entry for that day is... clean. Routine. No mention of anything unusual. But the very next morning, the Guild showed up with a half-dozen enforcers and a blacksmith, and they *welded* the lock mechanism shut. Filed the keyways, hammered the bolts cold.\"\n\nShe meets your eyes. \"So either Toran's logs missed something, or the Guild knew something he didn't. Or...\" she trails off, letting the implication hang.\n\nHer gaze drifts to the ink-stained clerk, who's pretending very hard not to notice you're talking about him. \"You want my guess? That ledger of his might have more in it than he's letting on. But he won't show it to just anyone.\"\n\nShe takes a slow drink. \"Think you can get him to open up?\""
    },
