      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the damp morning air, carrying across the field and echoing off the dark granite pillars.\n\n\"Old Bram!\"\n\nThe name hangs for a moment \u2014 then the mist swallows it. No answer from the void. The *Grey Hind* groans against the dock, a wet, wooden sound. Water laps at the pilings.\n\nSilence settles back in.\n\nBut something shifts at the edge of your hearing. Not a voice. Not footsteps. A faint *drip-drip-drip* from somewhere inside the gate's darkness \u2014 a sound that shouldn't carry, because the void between the pillars should absorb it. But it does. A single drop of water hitting stone, repeating at irregular intervals, as if something on the other side is wet and leaking.\n\nThe drip stops.\n\nThen starts again. Closer.\n\nYou're alone. The field is empty. The gate is sealed. But something on the other side just heard you call."
    },
