      "narrative": "You kneel, brushing the heel of your palm across the stone beneath the arch. Dust. Grit. A few loose pebbles. Nothing that suggests anyone's been here recently \u2014 no footprints, no scuff marks, no dropped objects. The dirt lies flat and undisturbed, as if the ground itself has been settled for days.\n\nYou squint, tracing the base of the right pillar where it meets the earth. The shadows pool thickly there, and you lean closer, but the light refuses to cooperate. Just stone. Just dust. Just the cold quiet of a place that's been locked up tight and left alone.\n\nA soft sound \u2014 the *Grey Hind* shifting against the dock. Water slaps the hull. Nothing else stirs.\n\nThe void between the pillars remains black and silent. Whatever it hides, the ground beneath your boots isn't giving it up."
